DOU-003 changes (2026-10-19): customs-legal 0.4.0 adds the
traveller-goods-documents skill preparing the documents for ordinary goods
carried by an adult traveller, for private use, arriving in metropolitan
France from a third country or a fiscally third territory: journey and
traveller sheet (stops, connections, likely place of controls, age,
residence), item-by-item inventory (bought during the trip, received as a
gift, already owned), questions on the non-commercial character, the
possible allowance and the declaration, missing documents. No allowance
granted or refused, no amount, conversion, declaration or sending; minors,
removals, vehicles, resale and regulated goods are detected and routed.
biens-voyageur.md 1.0.0 added with readings of 2026-10-19 (Directive
2007/74/EC, Regulation 1186/2009 art. 41, Delegated Regulation 2015/2446,
Implementing Regulation 2015/2447 on luggage controls and Union status,
Union Customs Code art. 15, 158 and 203, Regulation 2018/1672, recodified
French Customs Code as published on 2026-04-11, French tax code Annex IV
art. 50 octies, Code des impositions sur les biens et services art.
L. 213-33 in force on 2027-01-01, customs guidance pages). qualification-douanes.md 1.3.0,
envoi-outre-mer.md 1.0.1, import-document-checklist and
overseas-shipment-documents route travellers to the new skill.
