DOU-005 changes (2026-10-20): customs-legal 0.6.0 adds the
export-document-preparation skill preparing the documents of one ordinary
definitive export of Union goods by a business from metropolitan France to
an identified destination outside the Union: map of actors (seller, buyer,
exporter in the customs sense, declarant, customs representative,
carrier, consignee and end user) and of the operation, sale, transport and
exit documents received or missing, points to check for the product, the
destination and the end use, questions to the representative, the carrier,
the buyer or customs. The exporter and declarant are never inferred from
an Incoterm; an invoice without VAT or a transport document is not proof
of exit; dual-use, sanctions and sensitive end use leave the slice and are
routed; no declaration, licence, compliance, deadline, amount or VAT
exemption is produced or certified.
preparation-exportation.md 1.0.0 added with readings of 2026-10-20 (Union
Customs Code, Delegated Regulation 2015/2446, Implementing Regulation
2015/2447, VAT Directive 2006/112/EC, Dual-Use Regulation 2021/821,
Regulation 833/2014, recodified French Customs Code legislative part as
published on 2026-04-11, customs, DGE and Treasury guidance pages, TARIC and
Access2Markets as tools). qualification-douanes.md 1.5.0,
qualification-import-professionnel.md 1.0.1 and import-document-checklist
route exports to the new skill.
