DOU-006 changes (2026-10-20): customs-legal 0.7.0 adds the
tariff-classification-dossier skill preparing the classification file of one
good in the Union nomenclature, for import or export: structured product
sheet (description, materials and proportions, function, use, mechanism,
presentation, condition), missing technical attributes linked to the
document that would establish them, reasoned questions raised by a code
proposed by a seller, forwarder, carrier or tool, check of a binding tariff
information decision supplied (holder, goods, date of effect, scope) and
the official information route. The general interpretative rules are used
as a questionnaire, not a verdict; a composite set without established
proportions or main function keeps its classification reserved; a decision
for another holder or a neighbouring product is never transposed. No code
is settled, no rate, measure or amount is given and no request is filled
in or filed; origin and value stay separate.
